  "Main topic of the publication": "This paper investigates the evolutionary history of gene expression at the maternal-fetal interface, focusing on the transcription factor HAND2 and its role in pregnancy and associated disorders like preterm birth. The study suggests that HAND2 evolved uterine expression during the origins of pregnancy and may be important for maternal-fetal immune signaling and parturition.",
